# Infrastructure misconfiguration exceptions for the Infrastructure Scan gate.
# .github/workflows/iac-scan.yml runs `trivy config` over every Dockerfile,
# Compose file and infrastructure manifest in the tree and fails on MEDIUM and
# above; Trivy auto-discovers this file at the repository root, so a local run
# of the same command applies the same policy.
#
# EXCEPTION PROCESS - accepted findings go below, one check id per line. Every
# entry MUST carry a comment with: the reason it is acceptable, an owner, and an
# expiry date at which it must be re-reviewed. An exception without all three is
# not an exception, it is a hole. Example:
#
#   # AVD-DS-0026 (no HEALTHCHECK) on the migration image: it is a one-shot job
#   # that exits, so a healthcheck has nothing to report. Owner: ankit-yc.
#   # Re-review by: YYYY-MM-DD.
#   AVD-DS-0026
#
# Prefer fixing the manifest over adding an entry here. This file is empty on
# purpose: nothing has needed an exception yet.
